# Data exports from `npm run backup`. Never commit these: the repository is
# public, and a dump contains member data.
backups/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The club's own data. NEVER COMMITTED — this repository is public.
#
# data/club/members.csv holds real names and email addresses; funds.csv holds the
# club's real opening balances; transactions.csv would hold its ledger. None of it
# belongs in version control, and personal data in a public repository cannot be
# recalled once pushed — a deleted file stays in the history.
#
# The `.example` files beside them ARE tracked, so a fresh clone still knows the
# column layout. Copy an example to the real name and fill it in:
#
#   cp data/club/members.csv.example data/club/members.csv
#
# The live copy of all of this is the Appwrite database. Backups belong in Google
# Drive via `bash scripts/backup-to-drive.sh`, never here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/club/*.csv
!data/club/*.csv.example

# Google Drive for Desktop staging directories. This folder is synced by Drive,
# which writes .tmp.driveupload while uploading — thousands of files that a
# `git add -A` will otherwise stage, and whose contents are whatever Drive
# happened to be uploading.
.tmp.driveupload/
.tmp.drivedownload/
.shortcut-targets-by-id/
